        "Linear Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "Linear Regression is a supervised machine learning algorithm used for prediction and analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "It is applied when the target variable to be predicted is a continuous numerical value.\n",
        "\n",
        "The algorithm models the relationship between one or more input features and a single output variable.\n",
        "\n",
        "It assumes that the relationship between inputs and output can be represented by a straight line.\n",
        "\n",
        "The predicted output is computed as a weighted sum of input features plus a bias term.\n",
        "\n",
        "The primary goal is to find the best-fitting line that minimizes prediction error.\n",
        "\n",
        "During training, the model learns optimal values for weights and bias.\n",
        "\n",
        "Error minimization is achieved by reducing the difference between predicted and actual values.\n",
        "\n",
        "Mean Squared Error (MSE) is commonly used as the loss function.\n",
        "\n",
        "Linear Regression assumes independent errors with constant variance and normal distribution.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model is simple, computationally efficient, and easy to interpret.\n",
        "\n",
        "It is widely used in finance, economics, healthcare, and engineering applications.\n",
        "\n",
        "Common use cases include house price prediction, salary estimation, sales forecasting, and trend analysis.\n",
        "\n",
        "However, it is sensitive to outliers and performs poorly for non-linear relationships.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Logistic Regression\n",
        "\n",
        "Logistic Regression is a supervised learning algorithm used mainly for classification problems.\n",
        "\n",
        "It is most commonly applied to binary classification tasks.\n",
        "\n",
        "Despite its name, it does not predict continuous values.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model estimates the probability of an input belonging to a particular class.\n",
        "\n",
        "It first computes a linear combination of the input features.\n",
        "\n",
        "This value is passed through a sigmoid (logistic) function.\n",
        "\n",
        "The sigmoid function maps the output to a probability between 0 and 1.\n",
        "\n",
        "A threshold value, usually 0.5, is used to assign class labels.\n",
        "\n",
        "Logistic Regression is trained using log loss or binary cross-entropy loss.\n",
        "\n",
        "The loss function measures how close predicted probabilities are to actual class labels.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model assumes a linear relationship between features and the log-odds of the outcome.\n",
        "\n",
        "It is efficient, interpretable, and easy to implement.\n",
        "\n",
        "Logistic Regression is widely used in spam detection, disease prediction, fraud detection, and credit scoring.\n",
        "\n",
        "It can be extended to multi-class classification using One-vs-Rest or Softmax techniques."
